messages:
anita: FYI CS reported multiple new users hitting our JS quickstart and seeing opaque `Error: Bad request` in the console. Go/Python SDKs already show structured `InvalidArgument` errors with a friendly hint. We should fix quickstart + JS SDK sync.
cole: Oof. That kills first-time DX. Short-term: update quickstart to check `err.code` or `instanceof` instead of `err.type` which is Go-specific. Long-term: standardize wire envelope.
yasmin: Agreed. I propose a compact canonical envelope: `{code,human_message,hint,http_status,retry_after}` (minified on the wire). All SDKs parse that and surface typed exceptions.
greg: Streaming nuance: sometimes we close the stream with just a status. Two options: (A) include a final newline-delimited JSON trailer with the envelope, or (B) set `x-rw-error: 1` header and include a base64 JSON in `x-rw-err-json` on the final response. Prefer (A) for readability, but SDKs must fallback to status->code mapping when absent.
anita: Can we draft the mapping table now for docs? I'll paste a compact proposal: 400=InvalidArgument, 401=AuthenticationFailed, 403=PermissionDenied, 404=ResourceNotFound, 409=Conflict, 422=InvalidState, 429=RateLimit (include retry_after seconds), 500..599=ServerError (retriable).
yasmin: Yes. Also require `human_message` to be a concise, non-technical sentence (<=140 chars) and include suggested next steps when possible. No stacks. Server RFC will enforce.
cole: For the JS SDK: implement Error subclasses (InvalidArgumentError, RateLimitError, PermissionDeniedError, ServerError) with properties `code`, `humanMessage`, `hint`, `httpStatus`, `retryAfter`. Add a compatibility shim that maps legacy `body.message` -> envelope for one release.
greg: I'll draft the API change for streaming trailers and the header fallback. Include a tiny example for the dev docs.
anita: Quickstart snippet we should ship ASAP (replace old `err.type` guidance):
```js
try {
  await client.responses.create(req)
} catch (err) {
  // prefer instanceof checks, fallback to code string
  if (err instanceof InvalidArgumentError || err.code === 'InvalidArgument') {
    notifyUser(err.humanMessage || 'Your prompt is too long')
  } else if (err instanceof RateLimitError || err.code === 'RateLimit') {
    setBackoff(err.retryAfter || 60)
  } else {
    console.error(err)
  }
}
```

yasmin: Tests: add an integration that posts an oversized prompt to staging and asserts `err.code === 'InvalidArgument' && typeof err.human_message === 'string'`. Also add a streaming test that simulates a trailer and one that simulates no-body close to validate fallback mapping.
cole: I'll own JS PR (error classes + compat + linter rule that ensures constructed RedwoodError includes `code` and `human_message`). ETA: PR by EOD tomorrow.
greg: I'll own the server/trailer RFC and short API note for docs. ETA: PR by Thu.
anita: QA: I'll add the smoke test in sampleapp CI and coordinate CS to validate fixed tickets after deploy. qa-bot: Created task RW-ERR-2201 "JS SDK + quickstart error parity" assigned to cole, greg. https://github.com/redwood/devops/issues/2201
yasmin: One more: ensure 429 always includes `retry_after` (seconds) when possible; SDKs should expose it as `err.retryAfter` (number).
cole: Will add changelog note and a migration snippet for JS consumers. We'll keep the compatibility shim for one major release and log a warning when used.
anita: Great. Small, well-scoped win for onboarding. Post PR links here and CS will re-check impacted tickets after deploy. Thanks all :rocket:
